# Repos

Applies to every repo.

## Principles

- One source of truth for each fact. No copies. Mirrors are derived from the source, never edited.
- Minimal surface: fewest files, settings, and words that work.
- Self-contained. A template of this standard is part of it. No other outside dependency.
- No debris outside the repo unless explicitly allowed. Inside, debris only in `dump/`, including tool caches.
- Ordinary use offline. Network only to restore dependencies, or where the feature itself needs it.
- git. HTML for anything rendered.

## Track

- Authored source, durable records, dependency declarations, lockfiles, and declared deliverables.
- `scratch/`: tracked working material. Nothing outside it depends on anything inside it. Purging it leaves the rest unchanged. `scratch/README.md` states this.
- `scripts/`: repo-owned automation.

## Ignore

- Installed dependencies, environments, external binaries, caches, intermediates, and reproducible build output.
- Declared deliverables are the exception.
- `dump/`: all disposable work.
- `tools/`: external binaries. Track the versions, checksums, configuration, and scripts needed to restore them.
- Add a line only for a file this repo makes. No stock template.

Do not use `.work/` or `dump/gitignored/`. Both are `dump/`.
